      "updated": 1792156122758,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. All the local variable and parameters of stack are stored inside\nthe stack by compiler .\n\n2. Every stack uses stack for return address also .\n\nreturn address is the address of next statement to be executed\nwhen by every method call is over .\n\n3. Many application like browser uses stack to store history and\ntext editor uses stack for operation like undo .\n\n4. In DSA we use stack for problem solving , conversion expression\nfrom infix to postfix , implementing tree traversal technique .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. All the local variable and parameters of stack are stored inside the stack by compiler .\n\n2. Every stack uses stack for return address also .\n\nreturn address is the address of next statement to be executed when by every method call is over .\n\n3. Many application like browser uses stack to store history and text editor uses stack for operation like undo .\n\n4. In DSA we use stack for problem solving , conversion expression from infix to postfix , implementing tree traversal technique .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
